### Projection Alignment Table (INVARIANT)
Step IDs are semantic names, not positional labels.  The compact table
below is derived from the projection validation rules: exactly one row per
selected canonical step, in canonical order.  Use the exact `step_id`
values from the canonical projection; never a numeric position.

| canonical ID | action | executor | boundary | allowed narrative zone | allowed tree kinds | tree zone | bound resources |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
{% for row in projection_alignment_rows %}| {{ row.canonical_id }} | {{ row.action }} | {{ row.executor }} | {{ row.boundary }} | {{ row.allowed_narrative_zone }} | {% if row.allowed_tree_kinds %}{{ row.allowed_tree_kinds | join(', ') }}{% else %}empty set{% endif %} | {{ row.tree_zone }} | {{ row.bound_resources }} |
{% endfor %}

For every mapped leaf, its kind MUST be in the intersection of the
action-kind compatibility set and executor-role compatibility set shown in
its row's `allowed tree kinds` cell.

#### Boundary, zone, and binding rules
- An `external_precondition` leaf MUST have no zone.
- An `external_precondition` leaf may map only an outside-boundary canonical
  step.  Inside-boundary and crossing-boundary external preconditions MUST
  remain unmapped with empty `projected_step_ids` and realizations.
- A mapped leaf MUST use the resource bindings from its canonical step; never
  substitute a binding from another step.
- Internal and crossing mapped steps MUST use the canonical compatible zone.

#### Technique identity rules
- Technique IDs are optional annotations, but when present they MUST use
  either an ATLAS format (`AML.T####` or `AML.T####.###`) or a LAAF format
  (`S#`, `M#`, or `L#`).  Do not invent or rewrite valid technique IDs.
